"""Undercity: story speeches, and places named where the old accept line used to carry them."""

STORY = {
    'ucq_pd_ledger': ("It's Sennarath here. I've moved from ciphers to accounting, which I'd have found humiliating a year ago.\n\nI know the bribes can be traced, and here's why. The Blighted Courtiers of the Throne of Rot keep a ledger of every favour, given, received, owed and settled. It's the most meticulous document I've ever heard described, and it's kept by things that can't leave a room.\n\nThat's what court does to people. They kept a ledger alive, they kept it after they died, and not one of them has thought to stop.\n\nI want copies, in any condition. I can read through a stain. The Court of Rot is the north-west wing of the Plague Depths, below the iron door at the south end of the wheel. I'll set them against Wrenfall's lists and see whose names appear on both.", 'Bring every page, even the stained ones. The stains tell me which favours they handled most.'),
    'ucq_pd_vats': ("I'm Surgeon Halvard. Take a pair of gloves. I'm not asking.\n\nI need to see what the Society has been growing in the Vault of Flesh, and I need it from tissue rather than a report. A report tells me what somebody decided to write down. Tissue tells me how long they've been at it, and that's the real question. I can read it in the layering, the way you'd read rings in a felled tree.\n\nThe failed experiments carry fistfuls of it. They're still working out what they were supposed to be, which is the kindest way I can put it.\n\nThe Vault of Flesh is the east wing of the Plague Depths, through the iron door at the south end of the wheel. Keep your gloves on, and don't think about the faces. The ones who think about the faces come back with nothing usable.", 'Seal each sample in its own jar. If they touch, the layers blur and I lose the count.'),
    'ucq_hillsbrad_writ': ("The Executor signed a writ for the commander at Tarren Mill, and I drew it up for him. It gives her standing authority to act in the valley without writing north first. It sat on his desk for a month, because signing it meant admitting he can't run Hillsbrad from here. Take it south through Silverpine, down into Hillsbrad, and east to Tarren Mill, the mill town cut in half by a water channel, where Commander Thorne holds the line. The Executor would rather keep that authority for himself, and he signed it anyway, because the other choice was losing the valley by post.", "Keep it dry crossing the channel. A writ with the ink run is a writ she'll have to argue about."),
    'ucq_pd_noble': ("This one is distasteful, and I won't dress it up.\n\nThe Faulkner line was Lordaeron nobility, old, undistinguished and entirely legitimate. The last Faulkner was murdered in his bed, raised in a vat, and given a signet he doesn't remember owning. The Society made him the figurehead for the coup: a real name, a real line, and a man with no memory of either to contradict anybody.\n\nHe isn't guilty of anything. I want that on the record, because I'm about to ask you to kill him. He's also the legitimacy the whole conspiracy rests on.\n\nHe's in the Throne of Rot, the west wing of the Plague Depths. Take the signet off the body, and don't wear it, not even as a joke. Two people have, and I had to deal with both.", None),
    'ucq_pd_abomination': ("The samples point one direction, and I'd hoped they wouldn't.\n\nThey came from something in the vats, a single source at the heart of the Vault, and everything you brought me is a failed attempt at being it.\n\nIt's still growing. I've checked the layering four times because I wanted to be wrong. Whatever should have told it when to stop was never put in, or was taken out.\n\nI call it the Vile Plague Abomination. It doesn't recognise anything as a friend. It isn't hostile, it simply has no category for you. The Society's own people go into that chamber and don't come out, and I've got the tissue to prove two of them did.\n\nIt's in the deepest chamber of the Vault of Flesh, down in the Plague Depths. It's large, loud and wet. Bring a healer.", None),
    'ucq_pd_zulketh': ("Sit down with me. This is the last of it, and I want to say it in order.\n\nVex, the Noble, Voss and the Abomination were four limbs: a weaver, a figurehead, an archive and a weapon. That's exactly what a coup needs and nothing it doesn't.\n\nZul'keth is the heart. He's a Dark Sorcerer who believes the Dark Lady has failed us, rather than betrayed us, and that's why he's dangerous. A traitor can be bargained with. A man who thinks he's correcting an error can't.\n\nHe built a furnace of plague under this city to prove it, while we walked the wheel and congratulated a gatewarden on a quiet door.\n\nHe's in the Plague Heart, the deepest room of the Plague Depths. Everything you've killed down there was his. Go and finish it.", None),
}
